    <div style="background:#13233a;padding:20px;border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:20px;border:1px solid #24415f;">
    <h3 style="color:#7dd3fc;margin-top:0;">7. Worked Examples</h3>
    <p>The examples get harder as you go. Cover the solution, try the problem, then compare.</p>
    <div style="background:#0b1729;border-left:4px solid #22c55e;border-radius:9px;padding:16px;margin:16px 0;">
    <p style="margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#86efac;font-weight:bold;">✏️ Worked Example 1: Classifying <span style="font-size:12px;color:#0b1220;background:#86efac;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:999px;margin-left:6px;">Easy</span>
    </p>
    <p style="margin:4px 0;"><strong style="color:#fde68a;">Problem:</strong> Classify 2, 9, 23, 51 and 100 as even, odd and prime.</p>
    <p style="margin:8px 0;color:#cbd5e1;font-style:italic;">🧠 <strong>Thinking process:</strong> Check the last digit; then test primes.</p>
    <div style="background:#13233a;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;margin:8px 0;">
    <p style="margin:0;"><span style="display:inline-block;min-width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#38bdf8;color:#0b1220;font-weight:bold;margin-right:8px;">1</span><strong style="color:#bae6fd;">Step 1:</strong> 2</p>
    <p style="margin:6px 0 0 34px;color:#cbd5e1;"><em>Explanation:</em> Even and prime.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background:#13233a;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;margin:8px 0;">
    <p style="margin:0;"><span style="display:inline-block;min-width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#38bdf8;color:#0b1220;font-weight:bold;margin-right:8px;">2</span><strong style="color:#bae6fd;">Step 2:</strong> 9</p>
    <p style="margin:6px 0 0 34px;color:#cbd5e1;"><em>Explanation:</em> Odd, not prime (3 × 3).</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background:#13233a;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;margin:8px 0;">
    <p style="margin:0;"><span style="display:inline-block;min-width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#38bdf8;color:#0b1220;font-weight:bold;margin-right:8px;">3</span><strong style="color:#bae6fd;">Step 3:</strong> 23</p>
    <p style="margin:6px 0 0 34px;color:#cbd5e1;"><em>Explanation:</em> Odd and prime.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background:#13233a;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;margin:8px 0;">
    <p style="margin:0;"><span style="display:inline-block;min-width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#38bdf8;color:#0b1220;font-weight:bold;margin-right:8px;">4</span><strong style="color:#bae6fd;">Step 4:</strong> 51</p>
    <p style="margin:6px 0 0 34px;color:#cbd5e1;"><em>Explanation:</em> Odd, not prime (3 × 17).</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background:#13233a;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;margin:8px 0;">
    <p style="margin:0;"><span style="display:inline-block;min-width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#38bdf8;color:#0b1220;font-weight:bold;margin-right:8px;">5</span><strong style="color:#bae6fd;">Step 5:</strong> 100</p>
    <p style="margin:6px 0 0 34px;color:#cbd5e1;"><em>Explanation:</em> Even, not prime.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background:#052e16;border:1px solid #22c55e;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;margin-top:10px;"><strong style="color:#86efac;">✅ Final answer:</strong> Even: 2, 100. Odd: 9, 23, 51. Prime: 2, 23.</div>
    </div>
    <div style="background:#0b1729;border-left:4px solid #22c55e;border-radius:9px;padding:16px;margin:16px 0;">
    <p style="margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#86efac;font-weight:bold;">✏️ Worked Example 2: Is 97 prime? <span style="font-size:12px;color:#0b1220;background:#fde68a;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:999px;margin-left:6px;">Medium</span>
    </p>
    <p style="margin:4px 0;"><strong style="color:#fde68a;">Problem:</strong> Show that 97 is a prime number.</p>
    <p style="margin:8px 0;color:#cbd5e1;font-style:italic;">🧠 <strong>Thinking process:</strong> Test primes up to 9 (since 10 × 10 = 100).</p>
    <div style="background:#13233a;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;margin:8px 0;">
    <p style="margin:0;"><span style="display:inline-block;min-width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#38bdf8;color:#0b1220;font-weight:bold;margin-right:8px;">1</span><strong style="color:#bae6fd;">Step 1:</strong> ÷ 2</p>
    <p style="margin:6px 0 0 34px;color:#cbd5e1;"><em>Explanation:</em> Odd, so no.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background:#13233a;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;margin:8px 0;">
    <p style="margin:0;"><span style="display:inline-block;min-width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#38bdf8;color:#0b1220;font-weight:bold;margin-right:8px;">2</span><strong style="color:#bae6fd;">Step 2:</strong> ÷ 3</p>
    <p style="margin:6px 0 0 34px;color:#cbd5e1;"><em>Explanation:</em> 9 + 7 = 16, not a multiple of 3.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background:#13233a;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;margin:8px 0;">
    <p style="margin:0;"><span style="display:inline-block;min-width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#38bdf8;color:#0b1220;font-weight:bold;margin-right:8px;">3</span><strong style="color:#bae6fd;">Step 3:</strong> ÷ 5</p>
    <p style="margin:6px 0 0 34px;color:#cbd5e1;"><em>Explanation:</em> Does not end in 0 or 5.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background:#13233a;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;margin:8px 0;">
    <p style="margin:0;"><span style="display:inline-block;min-width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#38bdf8;color:#0b1220;font-weight:bold;margin-right:8px;">4</span><strong style="color:#bae6fd;">Step 4:</strong> ÷ 7</p>
    <p style="margin:6px 0 0 34px;color:#cbd5e1;"><em>Explanation:</em> 7 × 13 = 91, 7 × 14 = 98; no.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background:#052e16;border:1px solid #22c55e;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;margin-top:10px;"><strong style="color:#86efac;">✅ Final answer:</strong> 97 is prime.</div>
    </div>
    <div style="background:#0b1729;border-left:4px solid #22c55e;border-radius:9px;padding:16px;margin:16px 0;">
    <p style="margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#86efac;font-weight:bold;">✏️ Worked Example 3: Real-life operation <span style="font-size:12px;color:#0b1220;background:#fb923c;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:999px;margin-left:6px;">Hard</span>
    </p>
    <p style="margin:4px 0;"><strong style="color:#fde68a;">Problem:</strong> A school buys 1 248 books at Ksh 85 each and shares them equally among 24 classes. Find the total cost and the books per class.</p>
    <p style="margin:8px 0;color:#cbd5e1;font-style:italic;">🧠 <strong>Thinking process:</strong> Multiply for cost; divide for sharing.</p>
    <div style="background:#13233a;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;margin:8px 0;">
    <p style="margin:0;"><span style="display:inline-block;min-width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#38bdf8;color:#0b1220;font-weight:bold;margin-right:8px;">1</span><strong style="color:#bae6fd;">Step 1:</strong> 1 248 × 85 = 106 080</p>
    <p style="margin:6px 0 0 34px;color:#cbd5e1;"><em>Explanation:</em> Total cost.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background:#13233a;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;margin:8px 0;">
    <p style="margin:0;"><span style="display:inline-block;min-width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#38bdf8;color:#0b1220;font-weight:bold;margin-right:8px;">2</span><strong style="color:#bae6fd;">Step 2:</strong> 1 248 ÷ 24 = 52</p>
    <p style="margin:6px 0 0 34px;color:#cbd5e1;"><em>Explanation:</em> Books per class.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background:#052e16;border:1px solid #22c55e;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;margin-top:10px;"><strong style="color:#86efac;">✅ Final answer:</strong> Ksh 106 080; 52 books per class</div>
    </div>
    </div>
